Default tag catalogue and a tag form that shows what it means (1.7.0)

Only three status tags shipped, so a fresh install could not give a
project a status, tag a ledger row, or assign a member role. All 32
defaults now ship as a migration with names in nine languages, guarded per
slug so an operator's renames survive.

The form exposed none of the meaning the schema already carried:

- status_group was a free-text box with the placeholder `in_progress`.
  It is now a dropdown whose choices AND label change with the tag type —
  kanban column, pipeline tab, or accounting direction. The column is
  reused on purpose and its meaning has always depended on the type;
  nothing in the UI said so.
- is_closed and is_review had no control at all, so the app read columns
  nothing could set.
- Two of five grantable access categories were exposed.

Also: catalogue forms open in a dialog rather than expanding in place and
pushing the table out of view, and a swatch picker replaces the raw
colour input the browser renders as an oversized box.

